Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Outline", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"2e0882b1-c5ed-4188-a1a5-96324cb9cfd5"],

Cell["\<\
The main idea is to fit a curve to the number of active Bitcoin users \
(represented by active Bitcoin addresses), and then use that smoothed curve \
to fit Bitcoin\[CloseCurlyQuote]s value (represented by its Market \
capitalization), using a generalized Metcalfe\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law model.
Then we can see if Bitcoin\[CloseCurlyQuote]s market cap growth is in line \
with the growth in the number of its active users, according to Metcalfe\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law.
There are other applications in the paper that are out of scope / \
unimplemented for now (LPPLS model).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd6c9b7a-a612-48d5-8d00-523111e52e31"],

